WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.210
Picture two countries,
drawn as two stacks of bars.

2
00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:07.830
The first is wide at the
bottom, and narrows fast.

3
00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:12.270
The second is narrow at the
bottom, with a bulge near the top.

4
00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:17.630
Planners must decide what to build next,
and businesses must decide what to sell.

5
00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.190
So how can one chart
show a country's past,

6
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.190
and predict what its
people will need next?

7
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.070
In this mission, you'll learn
to read the chart's shape,

8
00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:28.380
from its base to its top.

9
00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:31.310
Then you'll compare places
at different scales,

10
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:34.310
from world regions to rural villages.

11
00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:39.510
Your mission: find out how one chart can
record a country's past and predict what

12
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:40.830
its people will need.
